WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.835
-Good evening. I'm Seth Meyers,
and this is "Late Night."

00:00:02.835 --> 00:00:04.169
How's everybody doing tonight?
That's great to hear.

00:00:04.169 --> 00:00:05.838
Let's get to the news.

00:00:05.838 --> 00:00:08.774
President Biden spoke yesterday
from the East Room

00:00:08.774 --> 00:00:12.011
of the White House and said
the situation in Afghanistan

00:00:12.011 --> 00:00:14.147
was "rapidly evolving."

00:00:14.147 --> 00:00:15.415
No kidding.

00:00:15.415 --> 00:00:17.950
Did you see what the Taliban did
in a weekend?

00:00:17.950 --> 00:00:19.319
Part of me's like,
"Put them in charge

00:00:19.319 --> 00:00:21.488
of the infrastructure bill."

00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:22.956
During his address yesterday

00:00:22.956 --> 00:00:24.690
about the situation
in Afghanistan,

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:25.959
President Biden attributed

00:00:25.959 --> 00:00:28.761
the Taliban's rapid takeover
of the country

00:00:28.761 --> 00:00:31.197
to a deal negotiated by
former President Trump

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.532
and the incompetence
of the Afghan military,

00:00:33.532 --> 00:00:36.703
but added
"the buck stops with me."

00:00:36.703 --> 00:00:39.772
Of course, before that,
the buck had quite a journey.

00:00:39.772 --> 00:00:41.941
"Really, it all begins when
George Bernard Reynolds

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:44.043
discovered oil in Persia
in 1908.

00:00:44.043 --> 00:00:45.544
Now, stay with me, folks."

00:00:45.544 --> 00:00:48.681
Former President George W. Bush
released a statement yesterday

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:50.516
about the situation
in Afghanistan,

00:00:50.516 --> 00:00:52.952
which is more than he did
in office.

00:00:52.952 --> 00:00:54.153
That's right.

00:00:54.153 --> 00:00:56.389
George W. Bush
released a statement yesterday

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:58.290
about the situation
in Afghanistan,

00:00:58.290 --> 00:01:01.861
and said he will remain
"steadfastly optimistic,"

00:01:01.861 --> 00:01:05.899
which, let's face it,
was always his thing.

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:08.300
CNN anchor Chris Cuomo
last night returned

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:10.603
from a week-long
regularly schedule vacation.

00:01:10.603 --> 00:01:12.505
Right. Regularly scheduled.

00:01:12.505 --> 00:01:15.742
Remember when COVID couldn't
even get this guy off TV,

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:17.476
but his brother resigns
and all of a sudden he's like,

00:01:17.476 --> 00:01:19.479
"Nobody likes a workaholic.
Bye!"

00:01:19.479 --> 00:01:21.881
[ Laughter ]

00:01:21.881 --> 00:01:25.251
New York City's vaccine
requirement for indoor venues

00:01:25.251 --> 00:01:28.154
like bars, restaurants, museums,
and movie theaters

00:01:28.154 --> 00:01:31.123
went into effect today,
so you can feel perfectly safe

00:01:31.123 --> 00:01:34.426
and then leave those places
and get on the subway.

00:01:34.426 --> 00:01:38.564
Former NFL quarterback
Jay Cutler was fired last week

00:01:38.564 --> 00:01:41.867
from an Uber Eats commercial
because of his anti-mask stance,

00:01:41.867 --> 00:01:44.403
so just like a Jay Cutler pass,

00:01:44.403 --> 00:01:46.973
that gig
is totally up for grabs.

00:01:46.973 --> 00:01:48.307
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.307 --> 00:01:50.476
Our resident Bears fan writer

00:01:50.476 --> 00:01:53.146
stills has some beef
with Jay Cutler.

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:54.647
[ Laughter ]

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:57.150
Today was
national Massachusetts day.

00:01:57.150 --> 00:02:00.119
Let me guess.
This calls for a drink?

00:02:00.119 --> 00:02:01.754
[ Laughter ]

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:05.524
A fan rushed the field at
the Mets/Giants game last night

00:02:05.524 --> 00:02:07.393
and stood
on the pitchers' mound.

00:02:07.393 --> 00:02:08.861
Thankfully, he was only able to

00:02:08.861 --> 00:02:11.864
strike out a few Mets
before he was apprehended.

00:02:11.864 --> 00:02:16.302
[ Laughter ]
Sorry, everyone on the crew.

00:02:16.302 --> 00:02:17.903
[ Laughs ]

00:02:17.903 --> 00:02:19.705
Police officers in Germany

00:02:19.705 --> 00:02:22.842
recently resuscitated
a Chihuahua using CPR.

00:02:22.842 --> 00:02:25.911
Sadly, no one was willing
to give mouth-to-mouth

00:02:25.911 --> 00:02:28.548
to the Saint Bernard.

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:30.449
And finally,
authorities in New York

00:02:30.449 --> 00:02:33.786
arrested a man yesterday
after he allegedly set 14 fires

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:35.922
across Manhattan
within a few hours.

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:38.357
The man is facing up to
10 years in prison

00:02:38.357 --> 00:02:41.327
and $1,200 in Uber fares.

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:43.763
And that was a monologue,
everybody.

